{
  "_comment": [
    "Australian hot-rolled steel section catalogue.",
    "",
    "=====================================================================",
    "THIS FILE CAN CHECK ITSELF, AND THAT IS THE POINT",
    "=====================================================================",
    "Every other reference file in this package holds values that can only be",
    "confirmed against the printed source. This one is different: it holds BOTH",
    "the dimensions AND the published properties of each section.",
    "",
    "Those two are not independent. The properties FOLLOW from the dimensions.",
    "So computing A, Ix, Zx, Sx, Iy, ry from the dimensions and comparing them",
    "against the published values is a real check -- a transcription error in",
    "either one shows up as a disagreement, and it would take a remarkably",
    "unlucky pair of errors to agree.",
    "",
    "Run it with:  austruct.sections.steel_catalogue.verify_catalogue()",
    "",
    "WHAT THE EXPECTED DISCREPANCY IS",
    "A rolled section has root radii where the flanges meet the web. This",
    "package models three rectangles and ignores them, so computed values are",
    "systematically LOW:",
    "",
    "  A, Ix, Zx, Sx   about 1-3% low. The fillets add material near the web.",
    "  Iy              under 1% low. The fillets sit close to the minor axis,",
    "                  so they contribute almost nothing to Iy.",
    "  J               10-30% low. Torsional stiffness is acutely sensitive to",
    "                  material at the junction, which is exactly where the",
    "                  fillets are. Do NOT use the computed J for design.",
    "  Iw              under 1% low.",
    "",
    "That pattern is itself diagnostic. A section whose Ix is 6% out has a",
    "transcription error; one whose J is 20% out is behaving normally.",
    "",
    "THE THREE-WAY AREA CHECK",
    "There are three independent routes to the area: from the dimensions, from",
    "the tabulated A, and from the tabulated mass divided by the density. Any",
    "two agreeing identifies the third as the outlier -- which turns 'these",
    "disagree' into 'the DIMENSIONS are wrong', and that is actionable.",
    "",
    "WHAT THE CHECK HAS ALREADY FOUND",
    "Every UB and UC in this file is internally consistent. Three channels are",
    "NOT: 100PFC, 125PFC and 200PFC have dimensions that disagree with their",
    "own tabulated area and mass. They are left as recorded, flagged, rather",
    "than adjusted to pass -- tuning the numbers until the check goes green",
    "would produce a file that is self-consistent and wrong, which is worse",
    "than one that is honestly broken.",
    "",
    "Channel I_w also runs 6-15% below the tabulated values across the range.",
    "That is a thin-walled formula meeting recalled data and either could be",
    "at fault; it is not localised the way the area check is.",
    "",
    "=====================================================================",
    "VERIFICATION STATUS",
    "=====================================================================",
    "Every dimension and every property below is RECALLED, not transcribed",
    "from a published table. Passing the cross-check means the dimensions and",
    "the properties are MUTUALLY CONSISTENT. It does NOT mean either is right:",
    "a whole section family misremembered consistently would pass.",
    "",
    "Before use: open the ASI or manufacturer tables and confirm the dimensions.",
    "The cross-check then confirms the properties for free.",
    "",
    "SCHEMA",
    "  designation  as written on a drawing, e.g. 310UB40.4",
    "  type         UB, UC, PFC",
    "  mass         kg/m",
    "  d, bf        overall depth and flange width, mm",
    "  tf, tw       flange and web thickness, mm",
    "  r            root radius, mm -- recorded but NOT modelled",
    "  published    the tabulated properties. null where not recalled; the",
    "               cross-check skips nulls rather than inventing a comparison"
  ],
